      <h4 class="section-label-x2">01 / Overview</h4>
      <p>
        As a federal contractor at the Indian Health Service (IHS)—a division of
        the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services (HHS)—for 11 years, I
        led and contributed to diverse, cross-functional product teams. My
        contributions spanned small-scale feature enhancements, custom graphics
        creation, and large-scale, nationally recognized digital redesigns.
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- Case Content -->
    <article class="case--content-block">
      <h4 class="section-label-x2">02 / IHS.GOV REDESIGN &bull; 2010 - 2012</h4>

      <p>
        Following an initial optimization of ihs.gov in 2009, I spearheaded a
        comprehensive redesign starting in 2010. This initiative launched just
        as the federal government began mandating Section 508 compliance for
        public-facing digital assets. The objective was to deliver a visually
        engaging, high-impact user experience while strictly adhering to 100%
        accessibility standards.
      </p>

      <p>
        By pairing robust backend architectures with cutting-edge front-end
        frameworks—including custom mobile layouts built on jQuery Mobile—I
        engineered a sustainable design framework that supported the agency for
        over a decade.
      </p>
    </article>

